15 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays a flow cytometry dot plot of CD3 versus CD19 from a co-culture, shown without blinatumomab \(BLN, grey\) and with 20 ng/mL BLN \(red\). Quadrant percentages are printed on the plot. Below, a paired dot-and-line plot shows the percent of residual CD19+ cells after 3 days with gamma-delta, CD4, or CD8 T cells \(grey=without BLN, red=with BLN\). Panel B shows four box plots displaying IFN-gamma, granzyme B, perforin, and granulysin concentrations \(pg/mL\); asterisks indicate statistically significant comparisons.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows dot plots of CD3 \(y\) versus CD19 \(x\) after 24 h co-culture with CD19+ targets, comparing Zole-expanded gamma-delta T cells \(green\) and PHA-expanded alpha-beta T cells \(grey\). Histograms below show CD3 signal. At right, plots showing percent residual CD19+ cells for NALM-6 and HAL-01 without BLN or with 20 ng/mL BLN. Panel B features box plots with IFN-gamma, granzyme B, perforin, and soluble Fas-L \(pg/mL\) for each target line; darker shades=without BLN and lighter shades=with BLN; asterisks indicate significant differences.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A features bar chart of residual CD19+ target cells \(%\) after co-culture under high or low CD19:CD3 conditions, measured at 24 h and day 3. Green bars show Zole-expanded gamma-delta T cells and grey bars show PHA-expanded alpha-beta T cells, each with no BLN, 0.5 ng/mL BLN, or 20 ng/mL BLN; donor values are dots and asterisks mark comparisons. Panel B shows overlaid histograms displaying CD3 mean fluorescence intensity at 24 h and day 3. Panel C features bar chart that summarizes normalized CD3 signal across groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (A three-part data visualization depicting immune cell analysis. Part A shows heatmaps of Vd2 and CD8 cells with various conditions and markers over time, indicating color-coded expression levels from low to high. Part B presents stacked bar charts of Vd2 and CD8 cell percentages categorized by naïve-like, CM, EM, TemRA, and all cells across different treatments and time points. Part C displays line graphs illustrating total Vd2 and CD8 cell counts over time with error bars, comparing different conditions including BLN and varying concentrations, under high and low CD19:CD3 ratios. asterisks indicate significant differences.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Two columns of line graphs track T-cell expansion in PBMC cultures from day 0 to day 7. Panel A plots absolute counts of Vdelta2+ \(top\), CD8+ \(middle\), and CD4+ \(bottom\) cells at days 0, 3, and 7. Panel B shows the same outcomes as fold change. Grey lines represent cultures without BLN and red lines represent cultures with BLN. Different point shapes indicate target-load conditions \(no added tumor cells, medium, or high\). Error bars show standard error of the mean; brackets with asterisks mark significant comparisons.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Panel A: Heatmap of selected genes \(rows\) across single T cells \(columns\), with annotation bars for sample, assigned cell group \(CD4, CD8, or gamma-delta\), and cluster number \(0\20513\). A UMAP \(2D map\) beside the heatmap shows the same cells colored by group. Panel B: UMAP compares untreated cells \(grey, no BLN\) with BLN-treated cells \(red, 20 ng/mL\). Panel C: Three UMAP feature plots show relative naïve, proliferation, and exhaustion scores on a color scale scale from minus one to two.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
